[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:22. A Glass Envelope]
[00:00.840]Passage 22 | 文章二十二
[00:02.470]A glass envelope. | 一封玻璃瓶信。
[00:05.780]My daughter Jane never dreamed of receiving a letter from a girl of her own age in Holland. | 我的女儿珍妮从没想过会收到一封来自荷兰，和她同龄女孩的信。
[00:14.300]Last year, we were traveling across the channel and Jane put a piece of paper with her name and address on it into a bottle. | 去年，我们坐船过海峡的时候，珍妮把一张写有她名字和地址的纸放进了一个瓶子。
[00:25.240]She threw the bottle into the sea. | 她把瓶子扔进了海里。
[00:28.660]She never thought of it again. | 她再也没有想起这件事。
[00:31.755]But ten months later, she received a letter from a girl in Holland. | 但十个月后，她收到了一封来自荷兰女孩的信。
[00:38.710]Both girls write to each other regularly now. | 现在两个女孩都定期给对方写信。
[00:42.880]However, they have decided to use the post office. | 然而，她们已经决定通过邮局写信。
[00:47.935]Letters will cost a little more, but they will certainly travel faster. | 信件的花费会多一点，但肯定会更快送达。